WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.584
Hannah: A representative workload includes callbacks. Include realistic reads and writes too.

2
00:00:07.584 --> 00:00:11.208
Raj: We'll dry-run it first without fault injection.

3
00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:17.281
Lukas: Then remove one zone. Use isolated production-equivalent infrastructure.

4
00:00:17.281 --> 00:00:21.865
Anika: Our working hypothesis needs cold-cache and retry coverage.

5
00:00:21.865 --> 00:00:25.705
Priya: Just to confirm, no customer traffic, right?

6
00:00:25.705 --> 00:00:30.433
Raj: Yes, sanitized data and simulated payment providers.

7
00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:34.225
Hannah: A smoke test precedes each load stage.

8
00:00:34.225 --> 00:00:39.002
Anika: Okay, measure order completion, not only response speed.

9
00:00:39.002 --> 00:00:43.322
Lukas: Perhaps record whether the capacity envelope actually holds.

10
00:00:43.322 --> 00:00:47.330
Priya: Yes, with abort thresholds agreed before testing.

